# ---- the square root ----
#
# Long division in binary, the way it is done on paper but in base
# four: two bits of the number come in, one bit of the answer goes
# out. Fifty-four rounds give fifty-four bits, which is one more
# than a double keeps, so the last one decides the rounding.
#
# The number is scaled to a hundred and eight bits, held as two
# halves, because a fifty-three bit fraction squared needs that
# much. The running remainder never passes twice the root, so it
# stays comfortably inside one number.
x_fsqrt m v:
